new file mode 100644
index 0000000..450fd75
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ON-DEMAND.md
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# Content-aware resource loading (local integration candidate)
+
+This patch is based on official `v3.0.0` (`07c18d120c43dd680390aebe112bd7c6a9565278`).
+It builds `3.0.0-demand.1` for Halo >= 2.27.0 and is not an upstream release.
+
+Set `basic.resource_loading` to `on_demand` in the plugin settings. The default `global`
+mode remains available for themes that require globally loaded resources. Frontend TeX
+rendering still follows `enable_frontend_katex`; the inline and display selectors apply
+only when that switch is on.
+
+An inline discovery script adds no KaTeX CSS/JS network requests on pages without formulas.
+Existing MathML/KaTeX output triggers CSS only and is preserved. Eligible raw formula
+nodes trigger the CSS then renderer, retaining source on failure. The loader never scans
+prose for delimiters. It skips code, existing rendered output and theme source controls.
+Invalid selectors are isolated. Formula errors use KaTeX's readable error output and
+`trust: false`; existing MathML is never replaced.
+
+## Navigation contract v1
+
+- Bootstrap: `script[data-katex-demand="1"][data-katex-version="3.0.0-demand.1"]`,
+  beginning with `/* halo-katex-demand:v1 */`.
+- Renderer: `script[data-katex-demand-resource="1"]` with the exact same-origin URL
+  `/plugins/plugin-katex/assets/static/katex.min.js?version=3.0.0-demand.1`.
+- `pjax:complete` and `katex:refresh` trigger discovery. `window.haloKatexDemand.refresh()`
+  returns a promise for the current attempt; concurrent discovery deduplicates nodes.
+- A theme replacing the document head must execute the next page's bootstrap after the
+  replacement so settings are refreshed. CSS removed with the old head is reattached;
+  the already loaded renderer is reused.
+- Emit `katex:suspend` immediately before committing a navigation. The next bootstrap
+  reactivates the loader; if the plugin is absent on the new page it remains inactive.
+- Detached nodes are not rendered after asynchronous resource loading. Failed resources
+  can retry on a subsequent refresh. `katex:resource-error` reports a resource failure.
+
+Do not indiscriminately allow arbitrary plugin scripts through PJAX. The companion theme
+patch recognizes only this explicit versioned contract and exact renderer URL.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+Use Java 21 and pnpm 10.20.0 (the repository's package manager version):
+
+```sh
+cd console
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm build
+cd ..
+./gradlew test build -x buildFrontend --no-daemon
+```
+
+The frontend is built explicitly before `-x buildFrontend`; the result is a full plugin JAR
+including editor frontend and KaTeX assets, not a backend-only substitute. Java dependency
+platform is the released `run.halo.tools.platform:plugin:2.27.0`. Devtools 0.8.0 supports
+Java 21 component indexing; Lombok 1.18.38 and the explicit JUnit platform launcher fix the
+old tag's Java 21/test-runner build incompatibilities.
+
+For independent HTTP/browser regression, provide an installed Playwright module and its
+browser cache, then run:
+
+```sh
+PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=/absolute/path/to/playwright/index.mjs \
+PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/absolute/path/to/browsers \
+node tests/on-demand.browser.mjs
+node tests/on-demand-race.mjs
+```
+
+2026-10-15 local checks: 4 Java tests and 2 deterministic late-failure race checks passed; 36 browser checks passed across Chromium,
+Firefox and WebKit using the actual bundled KaTeX assets. Cases include no formula,
+MathML preservation, raw inline/block formulas, disabled frontend rendering, malformed
+selectors, CSS/JS failure recovery, detached page cancellation, repeated refresh,
+head replacement, configuration updates and suspension. An isolated host thread context
+classloader test verifies that the embedded loader is read through the plugin classloader. These isolated fixtures do not
+by themselves establish Halo/editor/full-theme or physical Safari acceptance; record
+real Halo integration evidence separately.
